msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:31
msgid "Build polynomials"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:33
msgid "Use `from_coefficients` for a whole polynomial, and `constant`, `variable` and `monomial` for building blocks that you combine with operators:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:46
msgid "Trailing zeros are dropped everywhere, so `[0, 0, 0]` is the zero polynomial and `to_coefficients` always returns the shortest form."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:48
msgid "Read coefficients and degree"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:62
msgid "The zero polynomial has no degree, so `degree` returns `None` rather than `0`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:64
msgid "Do arithmetic without losing old values"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:66
msgid "Every operation returns a new polynomial; the operands stay as they were:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:80
msgid "`scale(k, c)` multiplies by $c\\,x^k$, and `pow(e)` is repeated multiplication done by repeated squaring."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:82
msgid "Evaluate, compose and differentiate"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:97
msgid "`p.substitute(q)` is the composition $p(q(x))$, so `moved` is $p(x + 1)$ and `moved.eval(1.0)` equals `p.eval(2.0)`. `derivative` is the formal derivative; here $p' = 3x^2 - 3$ vanishes at $1$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:99
msgid "Multiply long polynomials faster"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:101
msgid "`*` is the schoolbook product, $O(mn)$. For long operands call `karatsuba`, which gives the same result in about $O(n^{1.585})$:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:113
msgid "Below 33 coefficients in the shorter operand `karatsuba` simply calls `*`, so it is never slower in practice."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:117
msgid "Generic algorithms over coefficient types"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:119
msgid "Write algorithms with `luna-generic` bounds, re-exported by the facade, and they work for every coefficient type that has the capabilities:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:133
msgid "`UInt` coefficients work although `UInt` has no negation, because `*` and `eval` do not ask for one."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:135
msgid "Generic algorithms over representations"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:137
msgid "`DensePolynomial::ops()` packages the operations as a record, so the same code can run on the mutable representation too:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:152
msgid "Errors without aborts"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:154
msgid "`monomial`, `coefficient` and `scale` abort on a negative power. Their `_checked` forms return `None` instead:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:168
msgid "Powers through `arithmetic`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:170
msgid "`DensePolynomial` implements `@arithmetic.PowNatChecked`, so code written against `Luna-Flow/arithmetic` can raise polynomials to natural powers:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:185
msgid "**Coefficient order.** The array is ascending: `[a, b, c]` is $a + bx + cx^2$, not $ax^2 + bx + c$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:186
msgid "**`degree` of zero.** It is `None`. Use `length()` if you want `0` for the zero polynomial."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:187
msgid "**Fixed-width overflow.** `Int` coefficients wrap, and a leading coefficient can wrap to zero, lowering the degree:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:196
msgid "**Floating-point trimming.** Only coefficients that compare equal to zero are trimmed. `0.1 + 0.2 - 0.3` is not zero, so such a coefficient stays."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:197
msgid "**Derivatives need `NatHomomorphism`.** `derivative` works for `Float`, `Double` and `BigInt` coefficients; `Int` coefficients have no derivative."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:198
msgid "**`0^0`.** `pow(0)` returns one for every polynomial, including zero."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:199
msgid "**Printing.** `to_string` writes `x^1` explicitly and skips zero terms; use `to_coefficients` for exact output."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:203
msgid "The [immut/dense API](../../api/immut/dense.md) lists every method with its signature and cost."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/immut/dense.md:204
msgid "The [immut/dense design](../../design/immut/dense.md) derives Karatsuba, Horner and the Leibniz rule."
msgstr ""

